    "statement": "JIRA Issue: DOC-3181\n\nTitle: Rebuild Test Coverage Around Real Extension Behavior\n\nDescription:\nReplace placeholder tests and broaden coverage so the extension's core systems are tested through meaningful behavior rather than almost entirely through one feature area.\n\nProblem:\nThe repository has useful tests around codeLink, but coverage is uneven and src/test/extension.test.ts is still effectively a placeholder. Core lifecycle, provider, diagnostics, and workspace-loading behavior are under-tested.\n\nCurrent Evidence:\n- src/test/extension.test.ts\n- src/test/codeLink/*\n- src/test/misc/tagUtils.test.ts\n- src/test/pageLink/*\n\nScope:\n- Replace the placeholder extension test with meaningful activation/lifecycle coverage.\n- Add behavior-focused tests for plugin initialization and disposal.\n- Add tests for representative completion providers, diagnostics rules, and workspace loaders.\n- Strengthen failure-path tests for provider errors and file-missing scenarios.\n- Keep the project's existing Mocha + assert + sinon stack.\n\nOut of Scope:\n- Full migration to another test framework.\n- Snapshot-heavy or brittle implementation-detail tests.\n\nAcceptance Criteria: - src/test/extension.test.ts is no longer a placeholder. - Core lifecycle and at least 80 percent of representative providers per subsystem have meaningful tests. - Failure and edge-case scenarios are covered where behavior matters. - Tests remain readable and resistant to harmless refactors.\n\nValidation:\n- Run the full test suite locally.\n- Verify new tests fail before the implementation and pass after it.\n\nLabels: standards-alignment, vscode-refactor\n\nPriority: Not set\n\nWas this page helpful?: Helpful"
